    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35299" root="قدر" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِقْدَارٌ</span></b>  <i>A measure;</i> (JK, L;) <i>a thing with which
anything is measured;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَدَرٌ</span></b> : (L:) <i>a pattern</i>
(<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِثَالٌ</span>) <i>by which a thing is measured, proportioned,</i>
or <i>cut out.</i> (T, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مثل</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَدْرٌ</span>, in
six places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <i>Death.</i> They say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِذَا بَلَغَ العَبْدُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المِقْدَارَ مَاتَ</span> [<i>When man reacheth the term of life,
he dieth</i>]. The pl. is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَقَادِيرُ</span>. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُدْرَةٌ</span>.

